{
  "kanji": "湯",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 湯\ntitle: hot water\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [トウ]\nkunyomi: [ゆ]\ndistractors: [場, 油, 泥]\n---\n\n# 湯 — hot water\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n湯 means hot water and is also associated with baths and bathing facilities. It is not a generic spelling for water at any temperature.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture water beside a sun-like upper box with trailing diagonal strokes: the water has become hot.\n\nThe indexing radical 水 appears as 氵 at the left.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| トウ | on | 銭湯 せんとう - public bath; bathhouse |\n| ゆ | kun | [湯](../words/湯.md) ゆ - hot water; bath |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [湯](../words/湯.md) ゆ - hot water; bath\n- 銭湯 せんとう - public bath; bathhouse\n- [湯気](../words/湯気.md) ゆげ - steam rising from hot water; native-first mixed reading\n- [湯飲み](../words/湯飲み.md) ゆのみ - teacup\n\n## Notes\n\n- お湯 おゆ is the usual polite everyday form for hot water; お does not change the reading of 湯.\n- Compare [水](水.md), water. English 'water' can cover hot water too, but Japanese normally distinguishes 水 and お湯 in this temperature contrast.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1392420, 1448580, 1448600, 1612130.\n",
